# Task Completion Source-of-Truth

`Task.completedAt` is the **sole canonical indicator** of whether a task is completed.

## Rule

A task is **active** when `completedAt IS NULL`.  
A task is **completed** when `completedAt IS NOT NULL`.

Step completion state shows workflow progress but must **never** be used alone to classify a task as completed or to hide it from active views.

## Why this matters

`reopenTask` clears `completedAt` but intentionally leaves checked steps intact (audit trail). Any code that filters on step state will incorrectly treat a reopened task as still completed and make it invisible.

## Correct pattern

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT — matches backend query WHERE completedAt IS NULL
function isTaskComplete(task: TaskData): boolean {
  return task.completedAt !== null;
}
```

## Forbidden pattern

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG — hides reopened tasks where completedAt is null but steps remain checked
function isTaskComplete(task: TaskData): boolean {
  if (task.completedAt !== null) return true;
  const activeSteps = task.steps.filter((s) => s.status !== 'NA');
  return activeSteps.length > 0 && activeSteps.every((s) => s.status === 'COMPLETE');
}
```

## Applies to

- `JobTrackerShell.tsx` — `isTaskComplete()`, `counts`, `baseVisibleTasks`
- `page.tsx` — active task server query
- `actions.ts` — `getCompletedTasks`, `reopenTask`, any future filter
- Any new component that renders task lists or counts
